Revision 2 — 2026-05-15
=========================================================

Summary
---------------------------------------------------------
Fixed 7 issues from code review: signature mismatch, header
static cleanup, terminal buffer restore on quit, argv file
opening, safe allocator usage, status message impl, dead code.

Detail
---------------------------------------------------------

[1] include/fileio.h — editor_open signature mismatch
    Before : int editor_open(EditorConfig *ec, char *filename);
    After  : void editor_open(EditorConfig *ec, const char *filename);
    Why    : Definition in fileio.c used void and const, but
             header declared int and non-const — compile error.

[2] include/input.h — static declarations in header
    Removed: 5 static forward declarations for cursor movement
             functions and editor_quit.
    Why    : static in a header gives each includer a private
             copy — semantically wrong. These belong only in
             input.c where the functions are already defined
             static before their first use.

[3] src/input.c — editor_quit: restore main screen buffer
    Added : WriteFile(..., "\x1b[?1049l", ...) before exit.
    Why    : editor_init enters alternate screen (\x1b[?1049h)
             but editor_quit never exited it, leaving terminal
             corrupted after quit.

[4] src/Main/main.c — argv file-opening support
    Added : #include "fileio.h", argc >= 2 → editor_open()
    Why    : Editor could only create new files; running
             "TextEditor foo.c" was a silent no-op.

[5] src/render.c — abuf_append: remove unreachable NULL check
    Before : realloc() + if (new_ptr == NULL) return;
    After  : editor_safe_realloc() — no check needed.
    Why    : editor_safe_realloc exits on OOM, so the NULL
             check after it was dead code. Consistent with
             the rest of the codebase.

[6] src/editor.c — editor_set_status_message implemented
    Before : empty function body
    After  : vsnprintf into ec->statusmsg + time() stamp
    Why    : Function did nothing — status messages silently
             lost. Also added missing #include <stdarg.h>.

[7] Dead leftovers removed
    - TextEditor.h        (deleted): unused termios compat layer
    - src/fileio.c                  : duplicate semicolon ";;"
    - src/fileio.c                  : redundant safe_realloc comment

