Revision 5 — 2026-05-15 (Screen scroll fix)
=========================================================

Summary
---------------------------------------------------------
Fixed terminal scroll bug: status bar's trailing \r\n at the
bottom of the screen pushed all content up into scrollback,
making typed characters invisible.
---------------------------------------------------------
Detail
---------------------------------------------------------

[1] src/render.c — editor_draw_status_bar: remove scroll-inducing \r\n
    Before :
      abuf_append(ab, "\x1b[m", 3);   // reset attributes
      abuf_append(ab, "\r\n", 2);     // ← pushed cursor past last line → scroll!
    After  :
      abuf_append(ab, "\x1b[m", 3);   // reset attributes only
    Why    : After drawing content rows (screen_rows-1 lines) and the
             status bar on the last visible line, the trailing \r\n
             moved the cursor one line past the bottom, forcing the
             terminal to scroll the entire screen up. Every frame this
             pushed row 0 content into the scrollback buffer, making
             typed text invisible (though still present in memory and
             saved correctly). The cursor is repositioned by the
             subsequent \x1b[row;colH in editor_refresh_screen, so
             the \r\n served no purpose.

Affected Files
---------------------------------------------------------
  src/render.c            —  2 lines removed

