Revision 6 — 2026-05-15 (Backspace crash fix)
=========================================================

Summary
---------------------------------------------------------
Fixed editor_update_syntax calling editor_safe_realloc with
size=0 on empty rows, causing exit(1) on MinGW where
realloc(non-NULL, 0) frees memory and returns NULL.
---------------------------------------------------------
Detail
---------------------------------------------------------

[1] src/syntax.c — editor_update_syntax: handle empty rows
    Before :
      row->high_light = editor_safe_realloc(row->high_light,
                                             row->size);
      // memset + scan for digits...
    After  :
      if (row->size == 0) { free(row->high_light);
                             row->high_light = NULL; return; }
      row->high_light = editor_safe_realloc(row->high_light,
                                             row->size);
      // memset + scan...
    Why    : When a row becomes empty (e.g. deleting the last
             character), editor_update_syntax called
             realloc(non-NULL, 0). On MinGW (MSVCRT) this frees
             the memory and returns NULL, which editor_safe_realloc
             interpreted as OOM and called exit(1).
             The fix early-returns on size==0 after freeing the
             old highlight buffer, avoiding the zero-size realloc
             entirely.

Affected Files
---------------------------------------------------------
  src/syntax.c            —  5 lines changed

