Revision 9 — 2026-05-16
=========================================================

Summary
---------------------------------------------------------
Review cleanup: removed redundant HL_MATCH in editor_find, removed
dead row->index field, added save-fail feedback, enlarged terminal
seq buffer, allowed empty Enter in prompt.
---------------------------------------------------------
Detail
---------------------------------------------------------

[1] src/editor.c — editor_find: remove redundant HL_MATCH memset
    Removed: memset(&row->high_light[...], HL_MATCH, ...) after
             the search loop.
    Why    : editor_update_syntax already applies HL_MATCH globally
             to all matched rows. The per-row memset was redundant
             — it wrote the same value at the same location.

[2] include/common.h + src/editor.c — Remove dead row->index
    Removed: int index field from EditorRow struct, and all
             assignments to it in editor_insert_raw.
    Why    : index was maintained (set on insert, incremented on
             shift) but never read anywhere. Pure dead code.

[3] src/fileio.c — editor_save: error message on fopen failure
    Before : if (!fp) return;
    After  : if (!fp) { editor_set_status_message(ec, "Saved Failed! I/O error."); return; }
    Why    : Silent save failure misleads users into thinking the
             file was written successfully.

[4] src/terminal.c — Enlarge seq buffer from 4 to 8 bytes
    Before : char seq[4] = {0};
    After  : char seq[8] = {0};
    Why    : \x1b[1~ style sequences need 4 bytes minimum; the old
             4-byte buffer (incl. null) was too tight. 8 provides
             room for longer CSI sequences.

[5] src/editor.c — editor_prompt: accept Enter on empty buffer
    Before : if (buf_len != 0) { return buf; }
    After  : if (buf_len != 0) { return buf; } else { free(buf); return NULL; }
    Why    : Pressing Enter with empty search text previously did
             nothing, forcing the user to discover ESC exits.
             Now treated as cancel (same as ESC).

