Revision 10 — 2026-05-16
=========================================================

Summary
---------------------------------------------------------
Fixed cursor off-by-one caused by gutter_width not accounting for
the trailing space after line numbers. Fixed Enter-on-empty-file
leaving cursor past end of file (tilde lines + backspace no-op).
---------------------------------------------------------
Detail
---------------------------------------------------------

[1] src/render.c — gutter visual width mismatch (cursor off by 1)
    The line-number format "\x1b[36m%*d \x1b[39m" produces
    gutter_width + 1 visible columns (number field + trailing space),
    but all positioning code used gutter_width alone.
    Fixed 4 locations:
      - editor_scroll:   screen_cols - gutter_width
                         → screen_cols - gutter_width - 1
      - available_cols:  screen_cols - gutter_width
                         → screen_cols - gutter_width - 1
      - tilde width:     gutter_width - 1 → gutter_width
      - cursor position: cursor_x + 1 + gutter_width
                         → cursor_x + gutter_width + 2

[2] src/editor.c — editor_insert_newline: cursor past EOF on empty file
    Before :
      if (cursor_x == 0) {
          insert_raw(ec, cursor_y, "", 0);
          ec->cursor_y++;  // unconditional — broken when num_rows was 0
      }
    After  :
      if (cursor_x == 0) {
          insert_raw(ec, cursor_y, "", 0);
          if (ec->cursor_y < ec->num_rows - 1)  // content was pushed down
              ec->cursor_y++;
      }
    Why    : Opening an empty file (num_rows=0) and pressing Enter
             created row[0] but then cursor_y++ left the cursor at
             cursor_y=1 >= num_rows=1. This caused:
             - the second display line to render as "~" (no row data)
             - Backspace to silently return (cursor_y >= num_rows)
             - typing to create the row belatedly, fixing both issues
             The fix only advances the cursor when there is actually
             a row of content being pushed down.

Affected Files
---------------------------------------------------------
  src/render.c          —  4 lines changed
  src/editor.c          —  3 lines changed

